 paper's contribution is a calibrated negative/inconclusive measurement, a censoring-aware test design whose resolution limits are made explicit, and a clear list of what the evidence cannot say.\",\n  \"narrative_rationale\": \"The sealed final evaluation completed with outcome 'qualified' (final.qualification.outcome, status completed, correct true), so a paper about the measured results is supported. But 'qualified' certifies that the evaluation ran validly; it does not say the width hypothesis was supported. The decision rule fixed by the task contract (CI entirely below zero = supported, at/above zero = refuted, straddling = inconclusive) yields 'inconclusive' because the CI straddles zero. That is the most defensible and most honest story: a measurement-resolution paper. Alternatives rejected: (a) capacity-crossover / critical-width story (P1-P3 of the first model variant) -- no t_mem, t_gen, width-by-fraction or d*(f) results exist in the grounded artifacts; (b) lazy-to-rich or effective-learning-rate confound explanation -- the hidden-layer reparametrization sweep script was written but never executed (no code executed","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2479a9e-e8d3-4dec-9fbb-cae951098cd8","uuid":"3b7fbd62-9c02-4d75-86d2-ff412d888880","timestamp":"2026-11-11T14:26:21.352Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"@Article{Power2022GrokkingGB,\n title = {Grokking: Generalization Beyond Overfitting on Small Algorithmic Datasets},\n@Article{Furuta2024TowardsEI,\n title = {Towards Empirical Interpretation of Internal Circuits and Properties in Grokked Transformers on Modular Polynomials},\n@Article{Singavarapu2025InvestigatingTI,\n title = {Investigating the impact of low to moderate level label noise on Neural Network grokking dynamics},\n@Article{Nanda2023ProgressMF,\n title = {Progress measures for grokking via mechanistic interpretability},\n@Article{Dibiaggio2007DesignCV,\n title = {Design complexity, vertical disintegration and knowledge organization in the semiconductor industry},\n@Article{Wang2024GrokkedTA,\n title = {Grokked Transformers are Implicit Reasoners: A Mechanistic Journey to the Edge of Generalization},\n@Article{Thomas1976ACC,\n title = {A complex control circuit. Regulation of immunity in temperate bacteriophages.},\n@Article{Wang2024GrokkingOI,\n title = {Grokking of Implicit Reasoning in Transformers: A Mechanistic Journey to the Edge of Generalization},\n@Inproceedings{Simoes2014ModelingAA,\n title = {Modeling and Analysis with Induction Generators},\n@Article{Huang2024UnifiedVO,\n title = {Unified View of Grokking, Double Descent and Emergent Abilities: A Perspective from Circuits Competition},\n@Article{Penella2014ASA,\n title = {A simple and efficient MPPT method for low-power PV cells},\n@Inproceedings{Baeten2003AutomataLA,\n title = {Automata, Languages and Programming},\n@Article{Kumar2023GrokkingAT,\n title = {Grokking as the Transition from Lazy to Rich Training Dynamics},\n@Article{Graldi2025TheIO,\n title = {The Importance of Being Lazy: Scaling Limits of Continual Learning},\n@Inproceedings{Wang2024HowTG,\n title = {How Transformers Get Rich: Approximation and Dynamics Analysis},\n@Article{Mastrovito2024TransitionTC,\n title = {Transition to chaos separates learning regimes and relates to measure of consciousness in recurrent neural networks},\n@Article{Nam2024DecouplingDR,\n title = {Decoupling Dynamical Richness from Representation Learning: Towards Practical Measurement},\n@Inproceedings{Gheshlaghi2025AYLAAA,\n title = {AYLA: Architecting a loss landscape in shallow neural networks to accelerate feature recovery},\n@Article{Gowal2020UncoveringTL,\n title = {Uncovering the Limits of Adversarial Training against Norm-Bounded Adversarial Examples},\n@Article{Chen2020StabilizingDA,\n title = {Stabilizing Differentiable Architecture Search via Perturbation-based Regularization},\n@Article{Liu2022OmnigrokGB,\n title = {Omnigrok: Grokking Beyond Algorithmic Data},\n@Article{J